@@ -362,7 +362,7 @@ export const GLOSSARY_TERMS: GlossaryTerm[] = [
     shortAnswer:
       "Shingle curling is when the edges or corners of an asphalt shingle lift and bend away from the roof surface instead of lying flat, usually as the shingle ages and its asphalt dries out and loses flexibility. It shows up as either cupping, where the edges turn upward into a concave, bowl-like shape, or clawing, where the center rises while the edges curl downward or stay flat. Curling is a strong sign a roof is nearing the end of its service life and more vulnerable to wind and water intrusion.",
     body:
-      "A healthy asphalt shingle lies flat against the roof from edge to edge, sealed to the shingles around it and holding its shape through heat and cold alike. Curling is what happens when that flat, sealed profile starts to fail.\n\nThere are two recognized patterns. Cupping curl has the edges of the shingle turn upward, giving it a concave, bowl-like shape, and clawing curl has the center of the shingle rise while the edges curl downward or stay relatively flat.\n\nBoth patterns generally trace back to the asphalt losing the oils that kept it flexible, a natural part of aging that speeds up under prolonged heat, poor attic ventilation, or simply a shingle reaching the far end of its expected life.\n\nA curled shingle no longer seals tightly to its neighbors the way a flat one does, which leaves a lifted edge for wind to catch and a gap where wind-driven rain can work its way underneath more easily than on a flat roof.\n\nCurling tends to spread across a roof gradually rather than appear overnight, often starting on the slope that gets the most sun exposure and working outward from there as the rest of the shingles age at a similar rate.\n\nFor a homeowner, curling shingles are one of the clearest signs to look for from the ground when deciding whether a roof needs to be watched, repaired, or replaced.\n\nWidespread curling across most of a roof usually means the shingles as a whole are past their functional life, not a spot repair away from being sound.",
